WEBVTT

00:00:00.464 --> 00:00:03.622
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.622 --> 00:00:06.000
Being together like this...

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.878
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.878 --> 00:00:13.299
Forever...

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:15.801
...under this sky...

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.095
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.805 --> 00:00:21.098
In this beauty...

00:00:21.098 --> 00:00:22.224
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.224 --> 00:00:23.267
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:24.393
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.685 --> 00:00:26.020
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.104
...and more loving...

00:00:27.104 --> 00:00:28.188
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.188 --> 00:00:29.398
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.398 --> 00:00:30.649
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.899 --> 00:00:33.068
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.068 --> 00:00:35.738
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:37.948
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.948 --> 00:00:40.659
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.659 --> 00:00:42.703
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.703 --> 00:00:45.414
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.414 --> 00:00:47.541
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.541 --> 00:00:50.627
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.088 --> 00:00:56.467
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.802
If you go there...

00:00:58.802 --> 00:01:02.806
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.806 --> 00:01:06.185
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.185 --> 00:01:08.645
Under this sky...

00:01:08.645 --> 00:01:11.023
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:16.070
Being together like this...

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:19.573
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.285 --> 00:01:25.788
Under this sky...

00:01:25.788 --> 00:01:28.040
...we'll walk together!

00:01:31.147 --> 00:01:39.280
<i>After finding the unsolved Karuizawa Idol Murder case in the DDS
archive, I came to the scene to investigate during my vacation.</i>

00:01:40.073 --> 00:01:42.617
<i>The client was the victim’s sister, Reika Kurita.</i>

00:01:43.451 --> 00:01:47.246
<i>A couple of days ago, the older sister, Sumika,
had been found dead in a perfectly sealed room.</i>

00:01:47.914 --> 00:01:50.208
<i>However, shortly after we
started our investigation,</i>

00:01:50.208 --> 00:01:54.212
<i>we found her sister, Reika,
unconscious in the same room.</i>

00:01:55.088 --> 00:01:58.549
<i>Who is the perpetrator, and
what trick did he use?!</i>

00:01:59.384 --> 00:02:04.931
<i>But then he got to Yukihira, who
was investigating on her own.</i>

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:15.066
Please come to our show on stage one!

00:02:17.443 --> 00:02:19.904
<i>I wonder where Yukihira went...</i>

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.908
Hmm? Where's that smell coming from...?

00:02:30.373 --> 00:02:33.543
Damn, what's this?!

00:02:34.627 --> 00:02:38.798
That's a big thing of plastic...
so this is the source of the smell.

00:02:39.132 --> 00:02:40.883
You're not supposed to burn these...

00:02:41.175 --> 00:02:43.636
' Hey, you!

00:02:43.636 --> 00:02:45.471
Oh, Caretaker! This was...

00:02:47.265 --> 00:02:50.435
So, you put that in the fire! You brat!

00:02:50.852 --> 00:02:52.437
No, it wasn't me!

00:02:54.772 --> 00:02:57.775
So, you didn't burn this?

00:02:58.484 --> 00:03:00.903
Of course not! Why would I?

00:03:01.654 --> 00:03:05.533
<i>I see, this is what they used for the suffocation
trick in the sealed room.</i>

00:03:06.492 --> 00:03:10.621
<i>Wait a second then why did the perpetrator
rush to burn this in the incinerator?</i>

00:03:11.998 --> 00:03:14.042
Hey, what's wrong, Kid?

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:17.253
<i>Maybe someone got too close.</i>

00:03:20.339 --> 00:03:21.632
Yukihira and the perpetrator!

00:03:22.967 --> 00:03:23.843
Hey!!!

00:03:38.941 --> 00:03:41.069
<i>She showed off her DDS organizer.</i>

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:44.822
<i>It’s obvious that the perpetrator
was wary of Yukihira.</i>

00:03:45.865 --> 00:03:48.785
If she found any evidence...

00:03:49.911 --> 00:03:53.081
Megu! Yukihira was kidnapped and she's in danger!

00:03:57.418 --> 00:04:02.256
<i>Dammit, this is no good. If I wait for backup
to come from Tokyo, Yukihira will be killed!</i>

00:04:05.384 --> 00:04:12.016
Calm down, if I were Yukihira in this situation,
I'd do everything I could to leave a message.

00:04:13.392 --> 00:04:15.561
If she used the tools in the DDS organizer...

00:04:16.938 --> 00:04:21.943
No, if she was captured, her limbs were
probably bound, so she couldn't use the tools.

00:04:23.277 --> 00:04:28.699
Oh! She could still use the DDS watch,
even if her hands were tied behind her back!

00:04:29.951 --> 00:04:31.202
<i>Pursuit markers...</i>

00:04:31.869 --> 00:04:34.539
<i>Small paint balls fall to the ground and burst,</i>

00:04:34.872 --> 00:04:41.003
<i>creating an arrow out of fluorescent ink that you
can use to show your team members where you are.</i>

00:04:42.213 --> 00:04:42.922
Alright!

00:04:44.632 --> 00:04:46.342
If I follow these ink marks...

00:04:56.561 --> 00:04:59.772
<i>We stopped, where are we? What’s that sound?</i>

00:05:16.998 --> 00:05:20.459
Damn, where are they? I can't find any!

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:33.639
There's one! The ink contains
pheromones that attract butterflies!

00:05:35.725 --> 00:05:36.475
She's that way!

00:05:53.409 --> 00:05:54.285
HELP ME!!!

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.162
HELP ME!!!

00:05:59.916 --> 00:06:01.918
HELP ME!!!

00:06:02.084 --> 00:06:02.919
Yukihira!

00:06:09.091 --> 00:06:11.302
Ah, I can't swim!

00:06:14.055 --> 00:06:15.765
Damn it! Yukihira!

00:06:24.148 --> 00:06:24.857
Kinta!

00:06:26.859 --> 00:06:27.818
Grab my hand, Kyuu!

00:06:33.824 --> 00:06:34.659
Ryu!

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:37.078
Are you okay, Kyuu?

00:06:37.536 --> 00:06:39.163
Geez, why jump in when you can't swim?

00:06:39.372 --> 00:06:41.832
Megu, Kazuma... how...?

00:06:42.291 --> 00:06:46.003
We heard that you came to Karuizawa,
so we all came after you.

00:06:46.504 --> 00:06:49.840
Then I got your message on my voicemail,
and we all rushed to find you.

00:06:50.883 --> 00:06:53.678
But writing on that wall was the right thing to do.

00:06:55.054 --> 00:07:01.102
It'll catch attention, so somebody'd try to look
for you and it'd also lead us straight to you.

00:07:02.687 --> 00:07:04.897
Man, that was a close call.

00:07:07.608 --> 00:07:09.151
Kinta, how's Yukihira?

00:07:09.652 --> 00:07:11.153
She's just swallowed some water.

00:07:12.947 --> 00:07:14.407
Yukihira, are you okay?

00:07:17.076 --> 00:07:17.994
I'm so glad.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.959
I was so scared!

00:07:28.629 --> 00:07:31.090
Who'd have thought they'd get here before me?

00:07:31.966 --> 00:07:33.384
They're pretty good.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.143
It looks like Yukihira has calmed
down considerably.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.352
That's good.

00:07:43.853 --> 00:07:48.190
It's too early to relax, the
perpetrator is still out there.

00:07:48.774 --> 00:07:52.194
Yeah, you're right. We can't
leave things as they are.

00:07:53.154 --> 00:07:54.447
We have to do something quickly.

00:07:55.489 --> 00:07:59.201
Wait, Kyuu, are you saying that you
know who the perpetrator is?

00:08:00.661 --> 00:08:03.205
There's one person who's been -
exhibiting strange behavior.

00:08:04.373 --> 00:08:08.461
If it's due to the trick I'm
thinking about, it makes sense.

00:08:09.086 --> 00:08:10.379
What's that supposed to be?

00:08:14.425 --> 00:08:15.426
Yes, Toyama speaking.

00:08:17.011 --> 00:08:18.429
Headmaster Dan!

00:08:22.725 --> 00:08:26.479
Q-Class, I've been briefed on what
has happened up until now.

00:08:27.605 --> 00:08:29.148
Do you know who the perpetrator is?

00:08:29.148 --> 00:08:30.775
Yes.

00:08:30.775 --> 00:08:35.404
That sounds like a confident answer.
Have you secured any evidence?

00:08:36.322 --> 00:08:38.616
Unfortunately, I haven't had the chance to...

00:08:38.908 --> 00:08:45.498
Then I permit you to reveal that you're from
DDS and ask the police to officially aid you.

00:08:46.624 --> 00:08:49.960
Well, then, Q-Class, move out!

00:08:51.045 --> 00:08:51.712
Roger

00:08:53.381 --> 00:08:56.717
Officer, is it really true that
Reika's conscious again?

00:08:57.259 --> 00:08:59.470
Yes, it was only for a few minutes, though.

00:08:59.887 --> 00:09:00.971
I'm so relieved!

00:09:01.389 --> 00:09:06.894
I think she'll be ready to give some
sort of a statement by tomorrow.

00:09:07.603 --> 00:09:08.312
Excuse me.

00:09:25.955 --> 00:09:27.248
S-Sumika!

00:09:27.832 --> 00:09:29.583
I thought I killed you!

00:09:35.881 --> 00:09:37.550
So it was like that, after all.

00:09:38.509 --> 00:09:40.970
Oh, no, you can't escape anymore.

00:09:44.098 --> 00:09:45.683
Let's begin, shall we?

00:09:46.767 --> 00:09:48.519
The trick you used was pretty clever.

00:09:50.396 --> 00:09:54.900
The scene of the crime was
a perfectly sealed room.

00:09:55.317 --> 00:09:57.903
The windows had metal bars and the door was
locked and the dead-bolt was in place,

00:09:57.903 --> 00:10:00.322
...making entering the room impossible.

00:10:01.866 --> 00:10:05.411
The police couldn't do anything
but write it off as an accident.

00:10:07.371 --> 00:10:09.665
Then how did you figure out that it was a trick?

00:10:10.166 --> 00:10:10.833
Kyuu?

00:10:11.208 --> 00:10:15.463
Momo, I got that hint from the failed
murder attempt on Reika.

00:10:17.173 --> 00:10:22.595
The perpetrator forcibly tried to use the same
trick again, but made a couple of mistakes.

00:10:23.512 --> 00:10:26.807
One of them was that the room's
light was on the whole time.

00:10:29.059 --> 00:10:32.396
Because of that you left a certain
smell at the crime scene.

00:10:33.063 --> 00:10:33.689
Smell?

00:10:34.315 --> 00:10:36.484
You remember it, don't you, Yukihira?

00:10:36.942 --> 00:10:41.113
Yesterday, you said that there was a weird
smell when you entered the room.

00:10:41.989 --> 00:10:45.451
I smelled the same thing
at the incinerator today.

00:10:46.076 --> 00:10:47.536
It was the smell of burning plastic.

00:10:47.953 --> 00:10:49.538
I saw that, as well!

00:10:50.039 --> 00:10:54.835
And when I reached out to take a closer look,
I was hit by someone from behind and...

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.675
The big, plastic object that was being
burned in the incinerator...

00:11:02.092 --> 00:11:05.721
...was one of those big ad balloons
they use in the event hall.

00:11:07.348 --> 00:11:12.603
The perpetrator turned those into terrifying
weapons to kill people inside sealed rooms.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.939
What's that supposed to mean?

00:11:15.272 --> 00:11:16.982
Well, Kinta...

00:11:18.609 --> 00:11:20.486
Okay, please take a look at this.

00:11:21.195 --> 00:11:26.367
This little cage is the crime scene and
the quail egg inside is the victim.

00:11:27.201 --> 00:11:31.580
At first it seems impossible to crush the egg
inside the cage without opening the lid.

00:11:32.498 --> 00:11:38.837
But if you push the ad balloon, in this case a beach
ball, into the cage and inflate it from the outside...

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:42.841
...you get this...

00:11:45.344 --> 00:11:47.972
The same thing was done at the crime scene.

00:11:49.223 --> 00:11:54.687
Sumika suffocated because the ad balloon filled the
entire room, thus covering her mouth and nose.

00:11:55.854 --> 00:11:59.024
But it didn't work out so well in Reika's case.

00:12:00.067 --> 00:12:07.157
That's because the light she left on burned
the plastic and punctured the balloon.

00:12:07.741 --> 00:12:14.456
Maybe Reika half-believed that her sister
was really cursed to die...

00:12:15.416 --> 00:12:18.043
That? why she was afraid and went
to sleep with the light on.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:21.088
But because of that, she survived.

00:12:21.422 --> 00:12:25.676
And the perpetrator was afraid
that he'd be found out,

00:12:26.093 --> 00:12:28.804
...so he shoved the ad balloon
into the incinerator that night.

00:12:29.221 --> 00:12:32.850
But how did you figure out
who the perpetrator was?

00:12:33.559 --> 00:12:38.606
It was thanks to the strange behavior
the perpetrator exhibited.

00:12:39.148 --> 00:12:40.107
Behavior?

00:12:40.733 --> 00:12:42.401
Cut to the chase and tell us.

00:12:42.901 --> 00:12:45.696
This person here treated me like
the perpetrator, after all.

00:12:47.197 --> 00:12:48.991
It was the coat hanger.

00:12:50.701 --> 00:12:52.286
At first, I thought nothing of it,

00:12:53.454 --> 00:12:57.708
...but it was standing there Momos room
the entire time. That's when I noticed it.

00:12:59.001 --> 00:13:02.713
Those sharp hooks on the coat hanger
would have punctured the ad balloon.

00:13:03.797 --> 00:13:09.595
That's why you took the coat hanger out of Reika's
room when you came to check on her that night.

00:13:11.602 --> 00:13:13.646
You're the real perpetrator!

00:13:20.027 --> 00:13:22.071
You're the real perpetrator!

00:13:24.949 --> 00:13:25.866
You're not getting away!

00:13:26.617 --> 00:13:28.661
I'm right, aren't I, Manager Ooi?

00:13:36.585 --> 00:13:37.837
I can't believe it.

00:13:38.296 --> 00:13:40.506
Someone as kind as our manager...

00:13:40.881 --> 00:13:42.216
Why did you do it?!

00:13:43.551 --> 00:13:44.844
I hated them.

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.347
I hated those two so much
that I couldn't stand it.

00:13:51.267 --> 00:13:54.353
They killed my Misuzu! Those two did it!

00:13:57.064 --> 00:13:59.900
Then Misuzu Hikawa and you were...

00:14:00.609 --> 00:14:03.154
Yeah, we were lovers.

00:14:04.363 --> 00:14:09.660
But we had sworn to keep it a secret
until this event was over,

00:14:09.994 --> 00:14:12.163
until she was a full-fledged actress.

00:14:13.247 --> 00:14:14.206
And still...

00:14:15.791 --> 00:14:19.253
I'm sure I saw it! A white shadow by the window!

00:14:19.587 --> 00:14:21.130
Was it a ghost?

00:14:21.297 --> 00:14:22.673
That's just silly;

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:25.176
I've heard that this hotel is haunted.

00:14:25.968 --> 00:14:28.721
They say that there have been people
who were killed by the ghosts.

00:14:29.805 --> 00:14:31.849
Please, stop it, Sumika.

00:14:43.319 --> 00:14:44.779
M-Misuzu...

00:14:52.661 --> 00:14:55.623
If the girls hadn't started screaming,

00:14:56.332 --> 00:14:58.793
I would have lost myself and started ta cry.

00:15:00.544 --> 00:15:02.004
But I couldn't do it.

00:15:03.297 --> 00:15:06.342
Why didn't I stay by Misuzu's side
when she was scared stiff?

00:15:07.426 --> 00:15:10.596
Why couldn't I just hold her without
caring what others might think?

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:12.098
Why?

00:15:12.973 --> 00:15:15.810
That's when I heard it...

00:15:17.395 --> 00:15:20.231
...the truth behind Misuzu's death.

00:15:23.484 --> 00:15:26.278
I saw Misuzu! She was outside the window!

00:15:26.612 --> 00:15:29.532
Shh, calm down. You're imagining things.

00:15:29.949 --> 00:15:34.036
You're seeing illusions because you
think it's your fault Misuzu died.

00:15:34.286 --> 00:15:37.456
That was an accident, it wasn't our fault.

00:15:37.915 --> 00:15:44.130
But that girl slipped because we
were disguised as ghosts, and...!

00:15:46.465 --> 00:15:51.053
It's not like we pushed her down;
we've done nothing wrong.

00:15:51.554 --> 00:15:54.265
Just forget about Misuzu.

00:15:56.684 --> 00:16:00.938
What the hell is there to forget?!
They killed someone and they...

00:16:01.647 --> 00:16:05.901
Hey, Detective Boy, could you forgive them?

00:16:06.735 --> 00:16:11.365
Could you forgive someone who killed
the most precious person in your life?

00:16:16.954 --> 00:16:19.957
I don't think I could forgive them, either.

00:16:23.294 --> 00:16:28.174
But, still, I wouldn't kill anyone...

00:16:33.179 --> 00:16:35.347
Why don't we hear the rest of your
story down at the station?

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:36.765
Hey.

00:16:38.184 --> 00:16:43.606
What a foolish client! Admitting you're
guilty means that you'll lose your life.

00:16:50.738 --> 00:16:51.405
What's wrong?!

00:16:58.162 --> 00:16:58.954
Natsume!

00:17:03.709 --> 00:17:04.627
What did I do?!

00:17:06.587 --> 00:17:07.546
Call an ambulance, quickly!

00:17:08.047 --> 00:17:08.672
Yes, Sir!

00:17:09.159 --> 00:17:10.174
<i>This couldn't...</i>

00:17:09.548 --> 00:17:10.174
Mr. Ooi!

00:17:10.299 --> 00:17:10.466
<i>...be...</i>

00:17:10.466 --> 00:17:11.509
Hang in there!

00:17:11.759 --> 00:17:12.593
Mr. Ooi!

00:17:14.303 --> 00:17:19.058
I couldn't finish him off, but
the knife hit a vital spot.

00:17:24.813 --> 00:17:28.943
Geez, who in the world would lie
about my mother collapsing?!

00:17:33.364 --> 00:17:34.156
Hypnosis.

00:17:35.282 --> 00:17:38.702
You set up orders while your victim is asleep...

00:17:38.702 --> 00:17:41.163
Once awake, a certain event or keyword triggers
your victim to execute those orders.

00:17:43.165 --> 00:17:45.209
Making someone else finish your work,
so you won't soil your hands...

00:17:45.209 --> 00:17:48.879
your methods have always been dirty, Ms. Pluto.

00:17:51.465 --> 00:17:55.803
You know about us? Who the hell are you?!

00:17:56.136 --> 00:18:01.392
I guess I'll introduce myself.
I'm Morihiko Dan's right-hand man.

00:18:04.353 --> 00:18:06.897
I'm Koutaro Nanami from DDS.

00:18:07.565 --> 00:18:08.440
Kenzan!

00:18:10.693 --> 00:18:12.653
I won't let you get away, Pluto.

00:18:25.958 --> 00:18:26.959
<i>I’ve got him.</i>

00:18:28.002 --> 00:18:29.878
Urgh... just kidding.

00:18:30.629 --> 00:18:33.007
You're quite unladylike with
that knife, you know?

00:18:35.801 --> 00:18:36.719
And, there!

00:18:38.178 --> 00:18:40.055
I'm telling you, try being a little cuter.

00:18:42.016 --> 00:18:43.601
Hey, what's going on?!

00:18:47.062 --> 00:18:48.397
Is it sleeping gas?

00:18:51.984 --> 00:18:53.861
She cut the wire and fled?

00:18:54.945 --> 00:18:56.030
Damn, I failed.

00:18:58.699 --> 00:18:59.491
How are his Vitals?

00:18:59.491 --> 00:19:00.868
His blood pressure is decreasing.

00:19:01.452 --> 00:19:02.202
Give him a blood transfusion.

00:19:02.244 --> 00:19:02.578
Misuzu, where are you?

00:19:02.578 --> 00:19:03.954
Misuzu, where are you?
And give me...

00:19:03.954 --> 00:19:04.330
Misuzu, where are you?

00:19:04.371 --> 00:19:05.581
Doctor, his pulse...

00:19:05.581 --> 00:19:07.583
Misuzu, please answer me.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.418
Eijirou.

00:19:18.636 --> 00:19:19.470
Misuzu...

00:19:23.891 --> 00:19:25.893
Misuzu, what's wrong?

00:19:27.227 --> 00:19:30.731
I see, you can't stand the injustice, either.

00:19:31.482 --> 00:19:33.233
They intentionally did that to you!

00:19:34.318 --> 00:19:35.903
Please stop the hatred.

00:19:37.279 --> 00:19:37.905
Why?

00:19:38.697 --> 00:19:40.032
Why, Misuzu?

00:19:40.783 --> 00:19:42.993
Misuzu, why are you crying?

00:19:45.329 --> 00:19:46.038
Misuzu.

00:19:47.373 --> 00:19:48.123
Misuzu!

00:19:50.417 --> 00:19:51.752
<i>Mi...suzu...</i>

00:20:01.261 --> 00:20:01.929
Go ahead.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.644
You've all come.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:11.438
Manager Ooi!

00:20:12.272 --> 00:20:15.234
What's wrong? I guess it's weird that I'm alive.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:20.739
Manager, I still don't really
know what happened.

00:20:22.032 --> 00:20:24.159
I suddenly lost it and did-that...

00:20:24.952 --> 00:20:25.911
Don't worry about it

00:20:26.537 --> 00:20:28.622
I'm just glad you weren't found guilty.

00:20:29.707 --> 00:20:31.041
But more importantly, how's Reika?

00:20:31.583 --> 00:20:34.002
She's fine, and recovering nicely.

00:20:35.254 --> 00:20:37.047
I see, I'm glad to hear that.

00:20:38.006 --> 00:20:38.716
Mr. Ooi...

00:20:39.341 --> 00:20:45.180
It's kind of weird coming from the one who
tried to kill her, but I think that's great... now...

00:20:47.099 --> 00:20:50.102
I thought I was doing it for Misuzu,

00:20:51.103 --> 00:20:53.522
...but I realized that it wasn't really for her sake,

00:20:54.189 --> 00:20:57.109
...instead it was an act to satisfy my own hatred.

00:20:58.944 --> 00:21:01.739
Kyuu, thank you

00:21:03.407 --> 00:21:04.408
Ah, it was nothing.

00:21:04.575 --> 00:21:05.617
I'm so relieved!

00:21:05.617 --> 00:21:06.660
Me, too?

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.663
Excuse me, Mr. Ooi, may I ask you something?

00:21:10.289 --> 00:21:11.999
Um, you're?

00:21:12.541 --> 00:21:14.251
My name's Amakusa, from DDS.

00:21:15.377 --> 00:21:20.340
Did you know that Yukihira, who
was investigating with Kyuu,

00:21:21.049 --> 00:21:23.677
was seized, and almost killed by someone?

00:21:24.303 --> 00:21:26.889
What? I wouldn't go that far.

00:21:27.306 --> 00:21:27.931
I thought so.

00:21:28.682 --> 00:21:34.688
I've already found out that you had a meeting
with people from the movie industry.

00:21:35.564 --> 00:21:37.274
Amakusa, what's that supposed to mean?

00:21:37.775 --> 00:21:39.818
Who assaulted me then?

00:21:40.694 --> 00:21:45.991
Probably the one who hypnotized
Natsuki Yamasaki to stab Mr. Ooi.

00:21:47.785 --> 00:21:54.082
Mr. Ooi, won't you tell us the series of events that
took place before you committed this crime?

00:21:55.167 --> 00:21:59.338
You ordered a murder plan from a
certain organization, didn't you?

00:22:02.966 --> 00:22:07.095
I was about to turn crazy from all of the
hatred and anger that burned within me...

00:22:08.138 --> 00:22:13.393
One day, I found a small ad in the
paper and met with a counselor.

00:22:15.062 --> 00:22:17.981
What should I do now?

00:22:18.273 --> 00:22:23.612
Even if I sued those two, they probably
won't be charged with murder.

00:22:24.655 --> 00:22:26.031
What about Misuzu's loss?

00:22:27.032 --> 00:22:29.201
There's one good way.

00:22:30.702 --> 00:22:33.288
I'll introduce you to a certain organization.

00:22:33.956 --> 00:22:38.418
If you go to them, they will plan
a perfect crime for you.

00:22:39.503 --> 00:22:41.338
What I mean is, to kill them.

00:22:42.172 --> 00:22:46.677
The fee is half of all your assets,
due when the plan succeeds.

00:22:47.845 --> 00:22:49.012
How about it?

00:22:49.847 --> 00:22:55.853
When compared to the hell of living with that
gut-wrenching hatred for years and years,

00:22:55.853 --> 00:22:57.938
...it's not that expensive.

00:23:01.358 --> 00:23:03.944
So that's how it was. Thank you very much.

00:23:10.325 --> 00:23:13.161
What's this all about?

00:23:14.621 --> 00:23:15.998
Ryu?

00:23:19.084 --> 00:23:21.628
We should go back to Tokyo and
report to Headmaster Dan.

00:23:22.754 --> 00:23:25.048
That's the only thing we can do right now.

00:23:27.968 --> 00:23:35.100
<i>Ryu fell silent again, gazing into the
distance with a bleak expression.</i>

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.425
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.425 --> 00:23:49.761
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.761 --> 00:23:52.430
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.099
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.099 --> 00:23:56.101
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.101 --> 00:23:58.395
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.395 --> 00:24:00.939
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.939 --> 00:24:02.732
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.441 --> 00:24:06.987
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.987 --> 00:24:10.615
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.658 --> 00:24:13.702
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.702 --> 00:24:16.121
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.121 --> 00:24:18.248
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.248 --> 00:24:19.791
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.460
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.671
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.171 --> 00:24:26.881
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.881 --> 00:24:30.385
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.177 --> 00:24:33.346
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.346 --> 00:24:35.265
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.265 --> 00:24:37.642
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.684 --> 00:24:40.478
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:24:47.835 --> 00:24:50.129
Someone broke into Megu's house?!

00:24:50.880 --> 00:24:52.048
A deformed key hole...

00:24:52.632 --> 00:24:54.425
A strange feeling about the objects
missing from the room...

00:24:55.093 --> 00:24:56.844
Don't miss the intruder's tracks!

00:24:57.845 --> 00:25:01.057
Using Megu's memory as a clue we investigate the room.

00:25:01.641 --> 00:25:03.935
And the cornered perpetrator is:

00:25:04.614 --> 00:25:05.824
There's only one answer!

00:25:07.659 --> 00:25:09.869
I will acknowledge that you've won this time.

00:25:10.203 --> 00:25:12.163
But next time I will NOT lose!

00:25:12.789 --> 00:25:13.832
I wasn't really...

00:25:13.832 --> 00:25:15.542
No! It's a competition!

00:25:16.334 --> 00:25:21.172
Oh, if I win again next time,
will you show me your pan-!

00:25:21.172 --> 00:25:22.048
Idiot.
